      "key": {
        "uuid": "be6c098e_d73baace",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 746,
      "author": {
        "id": 1221725
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-20T00:39:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Haha, I saw that one, but it only goes to the end of the bitset, (and I think expanding it if needed.) Since our range was finite, and we needed it to wrap around (in case one was freed in the meantime), it seemed to make sense to do it manually.\n\nEg, in a size 3 pool, the current code would do:\nreserve -\u003e checks bit 1 -\u003e Allocates bit 1\nreserve -\u003e checks bit 2 -\u003e Allocates bit 2\nreserve -\u003e checks bit 3 -\u003e Allocates bit 3\n\u003e\u003e release 2\nreserve -\u003e Checks bits 1, 2 -\u003e Allocates bit 2\n\nWhereas the bitset.nextClearBit would allocate a new bit 4",
      "parentUuid": "c770ecc4_629cce85",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 740,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 746,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "797665ed5a778eb848e96a042fa85c4b3bfd377d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
